    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Invoices are now built from line items. Each line has a description, a quantity and a price each, and the app works out the total. Both tests in `e2e/specs/acceptance.spec.ts` pass with `bin/e2e`.\n\n**What you'll see**\n- On a project's page, each invoice number is now a link (`invoice-open-<id>`) to a new invoice page.\n- The invoice page lists the lines, showing each one's quantity, price each, and amount (quantity \u00d7 price), with the total at the bottom.\n- While an invoice is a draft, the page has a form to add another line.\n- The stored invoice amount is recalculated on the server every time a line is added. So the project's invoice list, the all-invoices page and the dashboard all show the correct total, not just the invoice page.\n\n**Database** (`V10__invoice_line_items.sql`)\n- There is a new `invoice_line_item` table, and quantity and price must both be greater than zero.\n- An invoice's amount can now be zero, so an empty draft is allowed.\n- Each existing invoice gets one line called \"Invoice amount\" (1 \u00d7 its old amount), so existing totals don't change.\n\n**Server**\n- Two new endpoints: one fetches a single invoice with its lines, the other adds a line (`POST \u2026/invoices/{id}/line-items`). Only draft invoices can have lines added.\n- The test seed endpoint now accepts `lineItems`, and test reset clears the new table.\n\n**Changes to existing behaviour you should check:**\n- **The amount field on \"Add invoice\" is now optional.** Leave it blank to start an empty draft and add lines. If you do type an amount, it becomes a single \"Invoice amount\" line. If any other test expects an error when the amount is left blank, it will now fail.\n- **An invoice with no lines (worth $0) can't be sent.** The server refuses it.\n- **Lines can only be added, not edited or removed.** You didn't ask for editing, so I left it out.\n\nYour request said the server was OfficeFloor, but this app is Spring Boot (as `CLAUDE.md` says), so I followed the existing Spring code.",
